From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a private page's desk is current to an extension
 allowed in private windows

A private page is a tab of its profile's private desk, as an incognito
tab is of an incognito window. Chrome's current window for an extension
allowed in incognito is the last active browser of either profile, so
ChromeExtensionFunctionDetails::GetCurrentWindowController asks the
desk's hook with the function's include_incognito_information
(chrome/browser/extensions/domicile_desk_hooks.h, CurrentWindowFor).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extension_function_details.cc | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extension_function_details.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extension_function_details.cc
index dfedf25..98475c1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extension_function_details.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/chrome_extension_function_details.cc
@@ -39,9 +39,12 @@ ChromeExtensionFunctionDetails::~ChromeExtensionFunctionDetails() = default;
 WindowController* ChromeExtensionFunctionDetails::GetCurrentWindowController()
     const {
   // Domicile's engine fork: on a desk, the desk is the window. The shell's own
-  // window is not one, and its active tab is the shell.
-  if (WindowController* desk =
-          domicile_desk::WindowFor(function_->browser_context())) {
+  // window is not one, and its active tab is the shell. With a private page
+  // last focused, it is the private profile's desk, for an extension allowed
+  // in private windows.
+  if (WindowController* desk = domicile_desk::CurrentWindowFor(
+          function_->browser_context(),
+          function_->include_incognito_information())) {
     return desk;
   }
 
